import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.Cc8dJFaW.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-22","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-22"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-22.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-22.md","lastUpdated":1795348050000}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-22.md"};function o(s,e,l,c,d,p){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence-·-2026-11-22" tabindex="-1">Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-22 <a class="header-anchor" href="#agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence-·-2026-11-22" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence · 2026-11-22&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Core finding: retry authority, artifact versions and independent acceptance are connected but distinct governance boundaries. No trusted November 21 success record exists; this run backfills from November 20 without inventing a past report.</p><p>20 selected observations, five analyses; zero experiments, articles or formal development reviews. Merged does not mean released; upstream testing is not local validation.</p><h2 id="carryover-reconciliation" tabindex="-1">Carryover reconciliation <a class="header-anchor" href="#carryover-reconciliation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Carryover reconciliation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>2026-11-19 A1</strong>：Historical scoped completion retained; remainder pending; no new experiment.</li><li><strong>2026-11-19 A2</strong>：Pending; corresponding experiments not run; original scope retained.</li><li><strong>2026-11-19 A3</strong>：Pending; corresponding experiments not run; original scope retained.</li><li><strong>2026-11-19 A4</strong>：Pending; corresponding experiments not run; original scope retained.</li><li><strong>2026-11-19 A5</strong>：Pending; corresponding experiments not run; original scope retained.</li><li><strong>2026-11-19 A6</strong>：Pending; corresponding experiments not run; original scope retained.</li><li><strong>2026-11-19 A7</strong>：Pending; corresponding experiments not run; original scope retained.</li></ul><h2 id="fact-observations" tabindex="-1">Fact observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#fact-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Fact observations&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="o1-·-codex-required-hooks" tabindex="-1">O1 · Codex required hooks <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-·-codex-required-hooks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 · Codex required hooks&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T20:25:11Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Required checks can block continuation; continue remains default. PreToolUse blocks execution; PostToolUse withholds an already executed result, without undoing effects.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62831" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o2-·-codex-mcp-reply-identity" tabindex="-1">O2 · Codex MCP reply identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-·-codex-mcp-reply-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 · Codex MCP reply identity&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-22T02:21:50Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Reply POSTs accept 202/204 acknowledgements, preventing independently assigned matching JSON-RPC IDs from resolving local requests.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63075" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o3-·-codex-subagent-messaging" tabindex="-1">O3 · Codex subagent messaging <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-·-codex-subagent-messaging" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 · Codex subagent messaging&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-22T01:25:39Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Root and spawned-agent async user messaging have independent opt-ins; availability does not establish role authority or acceptance.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/63069" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o4-·-codex-recovery-and-policy-composition" tabindex="-1">O4 · Codex recovery and policy composition <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-·-codex-recovery-and-policy-composition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 · Codex recovery and policy composition&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T12:23:32Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Recover server replies after WebSocket write failures; retry discovery with per-context backoff; compose layered network rules with deny winning surviving-list conflicts.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62749" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o5-·-paperclip-exact-retry-authority" tabindex="-1">O5 · Paperclip exact retry authority <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-·-paperclip-exact-retry-authority" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 · Paperclip exact retry authority&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T15:53:09Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Consumed exact-chat Retry authority cannot be copied to a system replacement; wait for sandbox recovery shutdown and then recheck retry authority.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22414" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o6-·-paperclip-live-owner" tabindex="-1">O6 · Paperclip live owner <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-·-paperclip-live-owner" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 · Paperclip live owner&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T16:32:42Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Do not offer Retry because of a newer pre-start cancellation while another run owns the task; UI and endpoint share the observed run.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22428" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o7-·-paperclip-atomic-tool-profiles" tabindex="-1">O7 · Paperclip atomic tool profiles <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-·-paperclip-atomic-tool-profiles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 · Paperclip atomic tool profiles&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-21T03:02:55Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Publish tool profiles and selectors atomically so concurrent admission cannot read partial assignments; scope responsibilities per user.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22455" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o8-·-crewai-artifact-cache" tabindex="-1">O8 · CrewAI artifact cache <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-·-crewai-artifact-cache" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 · CrewAI artifact cache&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T12:34:33Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Disable save_artifact caching: rewriting the same path must save another version even with identical arguments, rather than return an old URL.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9595" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o9-·-crewai-redirect-and-webhook" tabindex="-1">O9 · CrewAI redirect and webhook <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-·-crewai-redirect-and-webhook" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 · CrewAI redirect and webhook&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T15:33:22Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Cross-origin redirects strip auth, cert, params and bodies; A2A HMAC rejects missing/empty secrets, while none mode remains valid.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9516" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o10-·-openhands-projects" tabindex="-1">O10 · OpenHands Projects <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-·-openhands-projects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 · OpenHands Projects&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T22:59:33Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Projects API, coordinator tools, member board, artifacts and memory are merged. Upstream live model/browser evidence covers stated core scope, not every feature or local validation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6602" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o11-·-openhands-independent-judge" tabindex="-1">O11 · OpenHands independent judge <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-·-openhands-independent-judge" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 · OpenHands independent judge&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-21T00:30:52Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Judge failure/timeout becomes Needs you rather than critic-based auto-resolution; coordinators never auto-resolve; removing members clears board tags.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/7038" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o12-·-openhands-pr-evidence-and-resume" tabindex="-1">O12 · OpenHands PR evidence and resume <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-·-openhands-pr-evidence-and-resume" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 · OpenHands PR evidence and resume&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-21T01:11:27Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Record member PRs from the creating call&#39;s own result, not viewed PRs; runtime-added MCP tool names persist across restart, shipped in 1.63.1.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6922" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o13-·-orkas-retry-membership" tabindex="-1">O13 · Orkas retry membership <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-·-orkas-retry-membership" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 · Orkas retry membership&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T22:27:03Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Reject retry when the original agent is no longer eligible; preserve failed reply/board for rebinding, rather than silently fall back to Commander.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/242" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o14-·-orca-handoff-and-target-boundary" tabindex="-1">O14 · Orca handoff and target boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-·-orca-handoff-and-target-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 · Orca handoff and target boundary&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-22T08:40:05Z · <strong>MERGED</strong></p><p>Notify askers when takers exit or coordinating chats are deleted/replaced; reject remote-looking skill-install flags that actually write locally. Merges verified, no local/phone trial.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/46837" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o15-·-agents-sdk-codex-preview" tabindex="-1">O15 · Agents SDK Codex preview <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-·-agents-sdk-codex-preview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 · Agents SDK Codex preview&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T20:51:28Z · <strong>RELEASED_PRERELEASE</strong></p><p>Released v1.0.0-alpha.1 from feat/simple-codex, embedding Codex Core 0.166.0 via PyO3. SDK tools, approvals and handoffs are supported; native approval ends the model call. GitHub-only wheels include Windows x64; alpha.8 checkpoints are incompatible and old approvals must finish there.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/releases/tag/v1.0.0-alpha.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o16-·-uniemployee-oauth-and-im" tabindex="-1">O16 · UniEmployee OAuth and IM <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-·-uniemployee-oauth-and-im" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 · UniEmployee OAuth and IM&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-21T02:29:53Z · <strong>RELEASED</strong></p><p>Released v0.25.0/0.26.0: OAuth/PKCE, encrypted tenant/user/connector credentials, native IM employee sessions with approvals/traces. Stable encryption key is required; disconnect deletes local credentials without provider revocation. Upstream tests not rerun locally.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/zj-unicom-ai/UniEmployee/releases/tag/v0.26.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o17-·-orca-product-delivery" tabindex="-1">O17 · Orca product delivery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-·-orca-product-delivery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 · Orca product delivery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-21T17:57:28Z · <strong>RELEASED</strong></p><p>Released v1.4.268/269: Bots support more agents; phone approvals and tool setup require matching mobile builds. Upstream product claims; license, installation and rollback remain unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/releases/tag/v1.4.269" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o18-·-beads-migration" tabindex="-1">O18 · Beads migration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-·-beads-migration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 · Beads migration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T21:56:01Z · <strong>RELEASED_PRERELEASE</strong></p><p>v1.4.0-rc.4 is a prerelease excluded from stable channels. Schema v74 migration is one-way; old binaries refuse the store and rollback requires restoring backup.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/releases/tag/v1.4.0-rc.4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o19-·-browser-use-judge" tabindex="-1">O19 · Browser Use judge <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-·-browser-use-judge" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 · Browser Use judge&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-22T03:30:41Z · <strong>RELEASED</strong></p><p>1.0.8 released: judge adds a turn to the same run, reusing provider cache to reduce trace billing; this does not prove independent acceptance. Includes headless device login and password-output suppression.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/releases/tag/1.0.8" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h3 id="o20-·-adk-in-place-child-retries" tabindex="-1">O20 · ADK in-place child retries <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-·-adk-in-place-child-retries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 · ADK in-place child retries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>2026-11-20T05:55:19Z · <strong>COMMITTED</strong></p><p>Static child failures retry in place without restarting finished siblings. Workflow retry_config becomes frozen and child policies override inherited policies; workflow timeout can still yield max_attempts squared executions. Breaking behavior changes do not eliminate duplicate effects.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/f04b5fe424dbe2c8368682b54bc40ba070a0148d" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-·-retry-needs-identity-resource-and-attempt-boundaries" tabindex="-1">A1 · Retry needs identity, resource and attempt boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-·-retry-needs-identity-resource-and-attempt-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 · Retry needs identity, resource and attempt boundaries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O5、O6、O13、O20</p><p>2026-11-19 A2/A4 remain pending. Test whether user Retry authority can transfer to replacements, whether an unstopped executor duplicates effects, and timeout/retry multiplication. Runtime enforces admission/stopping; investigate causal attempt receipts in FCoP without importing scheduling into its core.</p><h3 id="a2-·-prove-artifact-versions-and-independent-acceptance-separately" tabindex="-1">A2 · Prove artifact versions and independent acceptance separately <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-·-prove-artifact-versions-and-independent-acceptance-separately" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 · Prove artifact versions and independent acceptance separately&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O8、O10、O11、O12、O19</p><p>2026-11-19 A3 remains pending. Priority candidate: rewrite an artifact path, consume the exact version, and route failed independent judging to humans. Inject cache hits, missing artifacts and judge timeout. Same-run judge caching saves cost but does not establish independence.</p><h3 id="a3-·-governance-checks-can-themselves-fail" tabindex="-1">A3 · Governance checks can themselves fail <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-·-governance-checks-can-themselves-fail" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 · Governance checks can themselves fail&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O1、O2、O4、O7、O9、O16</p><p>Retain A1&#39;s historical scoped results, not rerun. A2 remains pending: distinguish pre-action fail-closed from post-action result withholding, which cannot undo effects; local OAuth disconnect is not provider revocation. Partial profiles, colliding request IDs and cross-origin credentials are experiment candidates.</p><h3 id="a4-·-employee-products-are-tightening-handoff-and-human-escalation" tabindex="-1">A4 · Employee products are tightening handoff and human escalation <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-·-employee-products-are-tightening-handoff-and-human-escalation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 · Employee products are tightening handoff and human escalation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O3、O10、O11、O13、O14、O16、O17</p><p>Paperclip stays main radar with high learning value and increased enterprise-recovery attention; Orkas adds identity continuity; Orca stays second-circle with stronger mobile/multi-host interest; UniEmployee adds a connector trial candidate. OpenHands is a framework/application comparison. Judgments do not change Registry or prove maturity.</p><h3 id="a5-·-include-integration-and-migration-in-experiments" tabindex="-1">A5 · Include integration and migration in experiments <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-·-include-integration-and-migration-in-experiments" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 · Include integration and migration in experiments&quot;">​</a></h3><p>O12、O15、O16、O17、O18、O20</p><p>2026-11-19 A5/A6/A7 remain pending: tool naming after restart, memory isolation, event disorder, phone install and rollback are untested. CodexProvider Windows wheels are an isolated trial candidate; test Beads one-way migration only on backed-up copies. Applicability/cost unmeasured; zero development reviews.</p><h2 id="synthesis-engagement-and-coverage-limits" tabindex="-1">Synthesis, engagement and coverage limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#synthesis-engagement-and-coverage-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Synthesis, engagement and coverage limits&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Retry should not copy consumed authority, caching should not swallow new artifacts, and failed checks should not masquerade as completion. These are scoped research judgments, not universal laws or local-defect findings. Engagement questions: how is pending acceptance preserved when a judge fails, and which stop receipt authorizes a retry? No comments sent.</p><p>Fresh main Registry: 47 researchers and 88 repositories after supplemental radar union. Query window 2026-11-20T03:18:05Z to 2026-11-22T11:43:31Z. Commits, issues and releases queried; issue/release collections limited to ten entries per repository, full pages are partial and do not close history. Orca commits remain paginated; TSA inaccessible; Superset redirect normalization incomplete. Prior historical/social/license gaps retained. No commits for Yue Zhao (赵越) auditable/grade does not establish no papers/social activity; writing routing changes in agent-config/anywhere-agents retained without claiming governance innovation. Other raw events still await classification; this is a selected research snapshot, not complete coverage.</p><p>Separately checked Cursor&#39;s official changelog and MCP blog: latest visible dates November 6 and 11, respectively, with no new item for this window. This does not exhaust 47 researchers&#39; X/profiles; two GitHub links are not two source types. Publication acceptance is recorded in run receipts and chat.</p>',106)])])}const g=a(i,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
